        "message": "LU-21230 tests: fix sanity-lnet/291,292 for conns_per_peer > 1\n\nsanity-lnet test_291 and test_292 fail on a node whose NIC reports\na link speed of 4 Gb/s or more:\n\n    test_291: failed to set conns-per-peer to 1\n    test_292: expected 2 tcp connections on port 7988\n\nsocklnd sets conns_per_peer from the link speed.  At 100 Gb/s it\nsets 4.  The tests expect 1 bulk connection, but socklnd makes\nconns_per_peer bulk connections to the acceptor.\n\nRead conns_per_peer from \"lnetctl net show -v\" and expect that\nnumber of bulk connections.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: ce7611a495c1 (\"LU-19139 lnet: add accept_port_bulk module parameter\")\nFixes: f85b9c621972 (\"LU-20770 lnet: bulk conns use accept_port by default\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I57b1804247886e381317f466367b07280db5096b\n"
      },
